firedamp
========

Methane plume aggregator. Maps satellite-detected methane plumes
alongside O&G infrastructure from the OGIM database, and offers a
per-plume AI source attribution (Gemma 4 via OpenRouter, grounded on
OGIM, OpenStreetMap, place name, wind, and an Esri imagery snapshot).

Live: https://research.datadesk.eco/firedamp/


Plume sources
-------------
- Carbon Mapper      satellite + aircraft hyperspectral (API)
- IMEO / MARS        UNEP methane plume database (web scrape)
- SRON               TROPOMI weekly plume CSVs (FTP)
- OGIM v2.7          global O&G infrastructure (Zenodo GeoPackage)


Repo layout
-----------
    web/             static frontend (no build step, no npm)
      app.js           map, binary parser, detail panel, AI client
      style.css
      index.html
      layers.js        custom overlays (?layer=<slug>)
      dataset.html     AI-attribution browser (not currently linked)
      vendor/          MapLibre, PMTiles, Inter font
    scripts/         Python ETL (uv-managed)
      fetch_carbon_mapper.py
      fetch_sron.py
      fetch_imeo.py
      build.py         aggregates everything into web/data/plumes.bin
      build_ogim.sh    OGIM GeoPackage -> PMTiles (slow, ~30 min)
      serve.py         dev server with HTTP Range for PMTiles
      vendor.sh
    worker/          Cloudflare Worker `firedamp-api` (see worker/README)
    data/            input CSVs and intermediates (gitignored)
    .github/workflows/
      deploy.yml          Pages on push to main
      update-data.yml     daily plume refresh
      export-analyses.yml daily D1 snapshot to latest-data release


Setup
-----
Requires Python (managed with uv). OGIM rebuild additionally requires
ogr2ogr, tippecanoe, and tile-join.

    make vendor        download vendored JS/CSS/fonts
    make serve         dev server on :8000


Pipelines
---------
    make data          fetch CM + SRON + IMEO, build plumes.bin
    make ogim          OGIM GeoPackage -> PMTiles
    make ogim-upload   upload PMTiles to GCS
    make rebuild       full pipeline: data + ogim + upload


AI source attribution
---------------------
Detail panels include a model-generated source attribution. Requests
flow through the Cloudflare Worker in `worker/`, which holds the
OpenRouter key as a server secret and caches every response in a D1
database. See worker/README for setup. The browser hits the Worker via
the URL in `<meta name="firedamp-api">` in web/index.html.

A separate browser at /dataset.html lists every cached analysis (live
in the source tree but not linked from the main UI yet — re-enable by
uncommenting the subtitle link in index.html and restoring the cp lines
in the two deploy workflows).


URL scheme
----------
    Map position     #map=<zoom>/<lat>/<lon>
    Plume permalink  #plume=<id>
    Custom layer     ?layer=<slug>
    Local Worker     ?api=local   (when running `make worker-dev`)


Deployment
----------
Push to main -> deploy.yml -> GitHub Pages. plumes.bin is pulled from
the `latest-data` GitHub Release at deploy time. update-data.yml
rebuilds plumes.bin daily. OGIM PMTiles are deployed separately via
`make ogim-upload` to gs://firedamp-data/.

When adding new web assets, add them to the `cp` line in both
deploy.yml and update-data.yml.


